course: dictionary
lesson: 3111
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. The word elder is a good example. Read this: «The elder brother, who had stayed at home, was angry that the father celebrated.» Here elder means older, because it compares two brothers.
explain: Elder can also be a noun for a person. In «At festive dinners even kids raise their juice and shout gānbēi! (cheers!), holding the glass a little lower than an elder's», an elder is an older person who is respected. The clue is the lower glass, which shows respect.
explain: Elder can also be a tree. Look at the words around it: white flowers and dark berries point to the tree. Always ask which meaning fits, then try it in the sentence to check.
fact: Elder means older, as in «my elder sister».
fact: Eldest means the oldest of three or more.
fact: An elder is an older person who is respected for their knowledge and wisdom in a family or group.
fact: In many cultures, including First Nations, Aboriginal and Maori communities, elders are respected for their knowledge.
fact: An elder is also a small tree with white flowers and dark berries, called elderberries.
exercise: «The elder brother was angry that the father celebrated.» What does elder mean here? | *Older | Taller | Youngest | Smaller
exercise: «Be polite to your elders.» What are elders? | Children who are very loud | *Older people who are respected | Dark berries | Small trees with white flowers
exercise: Which word means the oldest of three or more children? | Youngest | Elder | *Eldest | Tallest
test: Which meaning of elder is a tree? | An older person who is respected | *A small tree with white flowers and dark berries | A kind of bird | Older, as in «my elder sister»
test: In «holding the glass a little lower than an elder's», what does the lower glass show? | Anger at the dinner | *Respect for older people | That the elder is thirsty | That the glass is broken
exam: Which meaning of elder fits «the elder brother, who had stayed at home»? | A small tree with dark berries | Youngest | *Older, as in the elder of two brothers | A respected older person in a group
